{"title":"Career Roadmap · Research Assistant","role":"Research Assistant","summary":"A Psychology Research Assistant supports research studies involving human behaviour, cognition, development, mental health, education and social behaviour. Typical work includes literature reviews, participant recruitment, data collection, psychological assessments under supervision, data management, statistical analysis and research documentation.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Clinical / Counselling / Child Psychology"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"A Research Assistant role is distinct from a clinical psychologist role. A psychology graduate should not independently diagnose, treat or provide regulated clinical services unless they hold the qualifications and registration required for that jurisdiction and role."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","What to Build"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Psychology, research methods, statistics, academic writing"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Research internships, participant work, data collection"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Professional"},{"text":"Research coordination, statistical analysis, publications"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Clinical, counselling, child, cognitive or social research"}],[{"text":"2037–2040"},{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Senior research/project leadership"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Research Leadership"},{"text":"Principal Investigator, Research Scientist, Academic/Policy Research"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Psychology foundation"},{"text":"Developmental, social, cognitive, biological psychology"},{"text":"Literature summaries"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Study design, sampling, questionnaires, statistics"},{"text":"Mini research project"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Applied research"},{"text":"SPSS/R/Python, interviews, assessments, qualitative methods"},{"text":"Research internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Independent research"},{"text":"Dissertation, data analysis, academic writing"},{"text":"Research paper/poster"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Psychology Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a broad understanding of psychology before specialising."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to psychology"},{"text":"Biological psychology"},{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Social psychology"},{"text":"Personality psychology"},{"text":"Learning and memory"},{"text":"Emotion and motivation"},{"text":"Psychological disorders"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For the selected course, pay particular attention to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychopathology"},{"text":"Mental-health research"},{"text":"Assessment concepts"},{"text":"Treatment-outcome research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling theories"},{"text":"Therapeutic processes"},{"text":"Well-being"},{"text":"Behavioural interventions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Child Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive development"},{"text":"Emotional development"},{"text":"Social development"},{"text":"Attachment"},{"text":"Parenting"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Adolescence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Research Methodology"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important transition from psychology student → research professional."},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Hypotheses"},{"text":"Operationalisation"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Validity"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Inferential statistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"t-tests"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Chi-square"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Effect sizes"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to select:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cross-sectional studies"},{"text":"Longitudinal studies"},{"text":"Experimental studies"},{"text":"Quasi-experimental studies"},{"text":"Case-control approaches"},{"text":"Cohort studies"},{"text":"Survey research"},{"text":"Observational studies"},{"text":"Mixed-methods research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research question","Hypothesis","Study design","Sample","Data collection","Analysis","Interpretation","Publication"]},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative Research"},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly valuable for counselling and child psychology research."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Case studies"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Content analysis"},{"text":"Coding"},{"text":"Reflexivity"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NVivo"},{"text":"ATLAS.ti"},{"text":"MAXQDA"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research Ethics"},{"type":"p","text":"Students working with human participants must understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Anonymisation"},{"text":"Voluntary participation"},{"text":"Right to withdraw"},{"text":"Risk minimisation"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"Research integrity"},{"text":"Avoiding coercion"},{"text":"Ethical treatment of vulnerable participants"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Child Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Additional care is required when research involves:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Minors"},{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"Children with disabilities"},{"text":"Clinical populations"},{"text":"Vulnerable families"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the concepts of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parent/guardian consent"},{"text":"Child assent"},{"text":"Safeguarding"},{"text":"Confidentiality boundaries"},{"text":"Referral/escalation procedures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Actual institutional requirements should always be followed."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Research Tools & Applied Skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Statistical Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn at least one professional statistical environment."},{"type":"h","text":"Priority"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R"},{"text":"SPSS"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Additional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"scipy"},{"text":"statsmodels"},{"text":"Jupyter"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For research roles, knowing how to interpret statistical output is more important than simply knowing software commands."},{"type":"h","text":"Research Data Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Data dictionaries"},{"text":"Coding variables"},{"text":"Missing-data handling"},{"text":"Participant IDs"},{"text":"Secure data storage"},{"text":"Version control"},{"text":"Reproducible workflows"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Basic SQL can also become useful for large research datasets."},{"type":"h","text":"Psychological Assessment Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Validity"},{"text":"Norms"},{"text":"Standardisation"},{"text":"Sensitivity"},{"text":"Specificity"},{"text":"Measurement error"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand major assessment categories:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive measures"},{"text":"Personality measures"},{"text":"Behavioural measures"},{"text":"Developmental measures"},{"text":"Symptom questionnaires"},{"text":"Educational assessments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not assume that learning about an assessment gives permission to independently administer or interpret restricted psychological tests. Use assessments only within the relevant training, supervision and institutional rules."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Research Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a research domain."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Psychology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Depression"},{"text":"Anxiety"},{"text":"Psychosis"},{"text":"Trauma"},{"text":"Addiction"},{"text":"Neurodevelopmental conditions"},{"text":"Treatment outcomes"},{"text":"Mental-health services"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling Psychology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stress"},{"text":"Coping"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"Well-being"},{"text":"Resilience"},{"text":"Academic adjustment"},{"text":"Career development"},{"text":"Counselling outcomes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Child Psychology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Parenting"},{"text":"Attachment"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Behaviour"},{"text":"Adolescence"},{"text":"School mental health"},{"text":"Neurodevelopment"},{"text":"Digital-media use"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Final-Year Research Project"},{"type":"note","label":"Example","text":"Academic Stress & Student Well-Being"},{"type":"h","text":"Research question"},{"type":"p","text":"What is the relationship between academic stress and psychological well-being among undergraduate students?"},{"type":"h","text":"Workflow"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Hypothesis"},{"text":"Ethical approval where required"},{"text":"Select validated measures"},{"text":"Define inclusion/exclusion criteria"},{"text":"Recruit participants"},{"text":"Obtain appropriate consent"},{"text":"Collect data"},{"text":"Clean dataset"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Interpret results"},{"text":"Discuss limitations"},{"text":"Write research report"},{"text":"Create poster/presentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final outputs"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research report"},{"text":"Dataset/codebook"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Research poster"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Potential manuscript"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This provides substantially stronger evidence of research capability than a purely theoretical project."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target internships as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Assistant Intern"},{"text":"Clinical Research Intern"},{"text":"Child Development Research Intern"},{"text":"Behavioural Science Intern"},{"text":"Cognitive Science Research Intern"},{"text":"Mental Health Research Intern"},{"text":"Social Science Research Intern"},{"text":"Academic Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Data Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Good environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology departments"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Research institutes"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Mental-health research centres"},{"text":"Child-development centres"},{"text":"Educational institutions"},{"text":"NGOs conducting behavioural research"},{"text":"Public-health research organisations"},{"text":"Clinical research organisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What to Do During a Research Internship"},{"type":"p","text":"Aim to participate in several stages of the research process:"},{"type":"h","text":"Before data collection"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature searches"},{"text":"Reference management"},{"text":"Study protocols"},{"text":"Questionnaires"},{"text":"Participant information sheets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During data collection"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Participant coordination"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Observations"},{"text":"Survey administration"},{"text":"Data entry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After data collection"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Coding"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Qualitative coding"},{"text":"Literature comparison"},{"text":"Research report preparation"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Biostatistics/statistics"},{"text":"R or SPSS"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Systematic literature reviews"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Good Clinical Practice where relevant to clinical research"},{"text":"Data management"},{"text":"Evidence-based practice"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certifications should supplement actual research experience, not replace it."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible early-career roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Psychology Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Coordinator"},{"text":"Project Assistant"},{"text":"Behavioural Research Assistant"},{"text":"Clinical Research Assistant"},{"text":"Child Development Research Assistant"},{"text":"Cognitive Research Assistant"},{"text":"Social Science Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research Data Assistant"},{"text":"Project Associate"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the employer and qualification requirements, graduates may also work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Behavioural research"},{"text":"Education research"},{"text":"Public-health research"},{"text":"Market/consumer research"},{"text":"Human factors research"},{"text":"UX research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers May Test"},{"type":"h","text":"Research methodology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How would you formulate a research question?"},{"text":"What is the difference between reliability and validity?"},{"text":"How would you select a sample?"},{"text":"What is a confounding variable?"},{"text":"What is the difference between correlation and causation?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"When would you use a t-test?"},{"text":"What does a p-value mean?"},{"text":"What is an effect size?"},{"text":"What is statistical power?"},{"text":"How would you handle missing data?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical research"},{"type":"note","label":"Scenario","text":"A participant withdraws halfway through a study."},{"type":"p","text":"The candidate should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respecting withdrawal"},{"text":"Following the approved protocol"},{"text":"Data-handling rules"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Escalation to the supervisor where required"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For long-term research careers, postgraduate study is strongly recommended."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful options include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Psychology"},{"text":"M.A. Psychology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Clinical Psychology"},{"text":"M.A. Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Child Psychology/Developmental Psychology where available"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research-related fields"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Cognitive Science"},{"text":"M.Sc. Neuroscience"},{"text":"M.Sc. Behavioural Science"},{"text":"M.Sc. Applied Psychology"},{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Epidemiology"},{"text":"Biostatistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact title, eligibility and professional scope of psychology programs vary substantially between institutions."},{"type":"h","text":"Research Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc.","M.Sc./M.A.","Research Assistant/Project Associate","PhD","Research Scientist/Faculty"]},{"type":"p","text":"For serious academic research, a PhD becomes increasingly important."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Psychology Caution"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc. in Psychology followed by research experience does not automatically qualify someone to practise as a clinical psychologist."},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical practice, diagnosis and regulated professional titles depend on the applicable Indian professional regulations and recognised qualifications."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, students should distinguish:"},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"from"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"when planning their education."},{"type":"p","text":"For any regulated clinical pathway, verify the current requirements of the relevant Indian regulatory authority and institution before enrolling."},{"type":"h","text":"Government / Public-Sector Research Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible research environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Government research institutes"},{"text":"Public-health programmes"},{"text":"Child-development programmes"},{"text":"Education research organisations"},{"text":"Social-development projects"},{"text":"Mental-health research programmes"},{"text":"Policy research organisations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Project Assistant"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Project Associate"},{"text":"Research Fellow"},{"text":"Research Coordinator"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Recruitment requirements vary by project and institution."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant master's programs include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Developmental Psychology"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Neuroscience"},{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Social Research"},{"text":"Psychological Science"},{"text":"Child Development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For research-oriented applications, strengthen:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research experience"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Research proposal"},{"text":"Recommendation letters"},{"text":"Research portfolio"},{"text":"Publications/presentations where available"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Academic Research Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Associate / Project Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Fellow"},{"type":"h","text":"PhD Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Postdoctoral Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Scientist / Faculty"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Management Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Coordinator","Senior Research Coordinator","Research Project Manager","Research Programme Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Research Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"flow","items":["Clinical Research Coordinator","Clinical Research Associate","Clinical Research Manager","Clinical Project Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"Additional clinical-research qualifications and experience may be required depending on the role."},{"type":"h","text":"Data & Behavioural Science Route"},{"type":"p","text":"A psychology graduate who develops strong quantitative skills can move toward:"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"flow","items":["Behavioural Data Analyst","Behavioural Scientist","Senior Behavioural Scientist","Research Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Skills required:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Experimentation"},{"text":"Survey methodology"},{"text":"A/B testing"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Experimental design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Psychology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"AI creates an important new research pathway."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Machine learning fundamentals"},{"text":"Natural language processing"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"Computational psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural data analysis"},{"text":"Digital phenotyping concepts"},{"text":"Experimental AI evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"Digital mental-health interventions"},{"text":"Educational technology"},{"text":"AI-assisted psychological assessment research"},{"text":"Computational behavioural science"},{"text":"Child interaction with digital systems"},{"text":"Cognitive modelling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI-generated conclusions should always be independently validated, especially when research involves mental health or children."},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Psychology research is likely to increasingly combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Behavioural science"},{"text":"Neuroscience"},{"text":"Digital health"},{"text":"Wearables"},{"text":"AI"},{"text":"Large-scale longitudinal datasets"},{"text":"Computational modelling"},{"text":"Natural-language analysis"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"Personalised interventions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest researchers will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Psychology","Research Methods","Statistics","Domain Expertise","Computing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Clinical psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Counselling psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Social psychology"},{"text":"Psychological assessment principles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Quantitative methods"},{"text":"Qualitative methods"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Research ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"R or SPSS"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Inferential statistics"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Effect sizes"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Reference managers"},{"text":"Qualitative-analysis software"},{"text":"Survey platforms"},{"text":"Git/GitHub basics"},{"text":"Research databases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Participant coordination"},{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Research posters"},{"text":"Scientific communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Systematic reviews"},{"text":"Meta-analysis"},{"text":"Behavioural data science"},{"text":"Computational psychology"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Psychology fundamentals + academic reading"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Research methods + statistics"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"R/SPSS + qualitative research + internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Dissertation + research presentation + advanced analysis"}],[{"text":"0–2 years after UG"},{"text":"Research Assistant / Project Assistant"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Research Associate / Research Coordinator"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Researcher / Research Fellow"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"PhD / Research Scientist / Research Manager"}],[{"text":"12–16 years"},{"text":"Senior Research Scientist / Faculty / Programme Lead"}],[{"text":"16+ years"},{"text":"Principal Investigator / Research Director / Professor"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Sc. Psychology + clinical/counselling/child psychology foundation + research methodology + quantitative and qualitative research + R/SPSS + Python basics + research ethics + academic writing + literature-review skills + 1–2 research internships + final-year research project + research poster/presentation + strong data-management skills."},{"type":"p","text":"For a long-term Research Assistant → Research Scientist pathway, the strongest next step after the B.Sc. is usually a research-oriented master's degree followed by specialised research experience and, for independent academic research, a PhD."},{"type":"p","text":"999 | UG | Science | B.Sc (General / Honours) | Sports Psychology / Sports Management | Sports Psychologist Assistant"}]}]}